WEBVTT

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:36.300
Damn it!

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:38.510
Don't be too reckless, Awin!

00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:40.060
The wheel isn't responding!

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:49.320
We can use that opening to reach the ruins.

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:51.480
I'm trying to, but...

00:00:59.000 --> 00:00:59.620
Escha!

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:08.710
Logy-san, there's the exit!

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:17.210
This is the Unexplored Ruins.

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:20.180
We actually made it!

00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:22.590
Yay! Yay!

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:27.200
We did it, didn't we, Logy-san?

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:29.550
Yeah, we did, Escha.

00:03:29.550 --> 00:03:31.030
We really made it.

00:03:31.030 --> 00:03:32.440
It's like we're in a dream.

00:03:35.770 --> 00:03:36.900
This is real, isn't it?

00:03:37.910 --> 00:03:39.530
Can you feel this?

00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:42.730
Thank you.

00:03:42.730 --> 00:03:43.880
What's wrong?

00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:48.410
I-I'll guard the airship, so don't worry.

00:03:49.190 --> 00:03:52.960
Linca-senpai is bad with heights.

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:55.980
If you go inside, it'll stop bothering you.

00:03:55.980 --> 00:03:56.670
That's right.

00:03:57.350 --> 00:04:01.220
You have to watch your step around here, so it would be safer to go inside.

00:04:01.460 --> 00:04:03.490
Eh? Is that so?

00:04:03.490 --> 00:04:05.850
In that case, let's get going!

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:11.270
Hey, Linca-san?

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:11.980
That's dangerous!

00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:20.860
Look at this!

00:04:20.870 --> 00:04:23.610
It's the first time I've ever seen such pretty berries.

00:04:24.070 --> 00:04:26.250
There's plenty of lush greenery around here.

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:29.450
It'd be worth investigating why there's so much food growing here.

00:04:32.890 --> 00:04:34.710
The ceiling is so high!

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:35.920
What could that be?

00:04:36.350 --> 00:04:37.920
Experimentation equipment?

00:04:39.810 --> 00:04:42.210
Doesn't something smell good?

00:04:42.210 --> 00:04:44.680
It smells like flowers, doesn't it?

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:51.640
The smell seems to be coming from this.

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:54.350
But what could it be?

00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:55.140
Wait!

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:56.600
Don't touch anything.

00:04:57.070 --> 00:05:00.220
Do you know anything about this, Threia-san?

00:05:00.220 --> 00:05:05.620
It's only a theory, but I think they were growing plants in this facility.

00:05:05.620 --> 00:05:07.560
This tube was probably used for that.

00:05:07.560 --> 00:05:08.620
Grow plants?

00:05:09.230 --> 00:05:11.700
Why up in the sky?

00:05:12.780 --> 00:05:14.410
This room is quite vast.

00:05:14.910 --> 00:05:16.730
These ruins are so large...

00:05:16.730 --> 00:05:18.420
How are they kept afloat?

00:05:22.980 --> 00:05:24.590
What is that?

00:05:29.150 --> 00:05:30.150
What?!

00:05:30.150 --> 00:05:31.440
A girl?!

00:05:31.690 --> 00:05:33.890
Who are you people?

00:05:34.260 --> 00:05:35.170
Huh?

00:05:35.170 --> 00:05:37.360
Where have I seen this girl before?

00:05:37.360 --> 00:05:42.030
We, um... came from Colseit to investigate these ruins.

00:05:42.460 --> 00:05:44.370
Colseit?

00:05:44.370 --> 00:05:46.490
I am Flameu.

00:05:46.490 --> 00:05:49.610
That is what you called me...

00:05:49.610 --> 00:05:51.680
But why?

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:53.200
I cannot recall.

00:05:54.100 --> 00:05:55.840
You said your name is Flameu right?

00:05:55.840 --> 00:05:57.790
What are you doing in these ruins?

00:05:58.870 --> 00:06:00.990
There was something I needed to do.

00:06:00.990 --> 00:06:02.230
A promise.

00:06:02.230 --> 00:06:03.710
Everyone's dreams.

00:06:03.710 --> 00:06:05.410
Everyone's hopes.

00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:07.220
For spring to bloom once more.

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:09.560
Spring to bloom?

00:06:09.560 --> 00:06:10.640
What are you talking about?

00:06:12.040 --> 00:06:14.010
It's almost done.

00:06:14.010 --> 00:06:16.140
So I won't let humans interfere.

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:18.730
I won't let humans have it.

00:06:20.090 --> 00:06:21.680
T-The ruins are...!

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:22.440
Escha!

00:06:23.350 --> 00:06:25.490
Please, Kuu.

00:06:25.490 --> 00:06:27.600
Lend me your power.

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:44.340
What's with that thing?

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:52.890
Listen, exterminate the humans!

00:06:54.100 --> 00:06:55.600
Leave this to me!

00:06:58.720 --> 00:07:00.810
I'll destroy it at once!

00:07:07.720 --> 00:07:08.820
It's powerful.

00:07:11.570 --> 00:07:13.320
Watch out!

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:20.370
Damn, there's no opening to attack!

00:07:24.460 --> 00:07:26.010
Our opponent is too strong!

00:07:26.010 --> 00:07:28.300
At this rate we're going to get wiped out!

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:30.080
We have no choice.

00:07:30.080 --> 00:07:31.020
Retreat!

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:34.010
Everyone, run back to the airship!

00:07:37.300 --> 00:07:38.850
Hurry!

00:07:47.290 --> 00:07:48.440
Release the anchor!

00:08:05.630 --> 00:08:06.590
It's chasing after us!

00:08:06.590 --> 00:08:07.710
Full speed ahead!

00:08:19.980 --> 00:08:21.480
I can't believe that happened.

00:08:22.390 --> 00:08:25.070
I'm glad you guys made it back.

00:08:25.070 --> 00:08:27.620
But to survey it again...

00:08:27.620 --> 00:08:30.140
What should we do, Branch Manager?

00:08:31.070 --> 00:08:33.990
Actually, Central City sent us a message.

00:08:33.990 --> 00:08:36.700
They said that their investigation had been cancelled,

00:08:36.920 --> 00:08:40.670
so there's nothing to stop us from investigating.

00:08:40.670 --> 00:08:43.210
To think the Unexplored Ruins were that dangerous.

00:08:43.210 --> 00:08:45.800
That girl especially bothers me.

00:08:45.800 --> 00:08:47.650
About that girl,

00:08:47.650 --> 00:08:51.170
I feel like I know her.

00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:54.970
It didn't feel like this was the first time we've met.

00:08:55.540 --> 00:08:58.650
A wave of nostalgia swept over me when I saw her.

00:08:59.210 --> 00:09:03.150
I actually think I've seen her before too.

00:09:03.150 --> 00:09:06.150
But where?

00:09:07.510 --> 00:09:08.730
Do you guys have a second?

00:09:09.050 --> 00:09:10.570
What is it, Threia?

00:09:11.150 --> 00:09:12.530
Take a look at this.

00:09:15.990 --> 00:09:17.690
This girl!

00:09:17.690 --> 00:09:19.460
This is it!

00:09:19.990 --> 00:09:23.370
This tablet was of that girl in the Unexplored Ruins after all.

00:09:24.350 --> 00:09:26.790
There's one more thing that caught my attention.

00:09:29.730 --> 00:09:31.130
T-This is...

00:09:31.690 --> 00:09:33.090
Clone?!

00:09:34.910 --> 00:09:38.850
My oh my, something like this still exists?

00:09:38.850 --> 00:09:42.350
I had thought they had already been lost.

00:09:42.350 --> 00:09:44.590
So it was Clone after all.

00:09:44.590 --> 00:09:47.230
We met a girl in the Unexplored Ruins.

00:09:47.230 --> 00:09:48.490
Eh?

00:09:48.490 --> 00:09:53.820
Hey Clone, why is she in the ruins?

00:09:53.820 --> 00:09:55.360
That's...

00:09:55.360 --> 00:09:59.280
Can you tell us as well?

00:09:59.960 --> 00:10:01.220
Nio-san!

00:10:01.220 --> 00:10:04.830
We finally figured out whose voice Nio's been hearing.

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:05.420
Eh?

00:10:05.640 --> 00:10:08.490
The voice belongs to Flameu.

00:10:08.490 --> 00:10:10.790
So please tell us as well.

00:10:16.010 --> 00:10:17.590
Understood.

00:10:17.590 --> 00:10:19.290
I shall tell you.

00:10:19.290 --> 00:10:24.620
It's an old record, so it may take some time.

00:10:34.890 --> 00:10:42.070
The place that you all refer to as the Unexplored Ruins is actually Geosys, a research facility.

00:10:44.130 --> 00:10:50.750
And Flameu is an alchemist born in the same era as I.

00:11:04.130 --> 00:11:06.520
She's an alchemist?

00:11:06.520 --> 00:11:08.600
What's this research facility you speak off?

00:11:08.890 --> 00:11:12.550
Back then, the Land of Dusk was already on the decline.

00:11:12.550 --> 00:11:20.610
Flameu gathered many peers in the facility and tried to find a way to save the land.

00:11:20.610 --> 00:11:21.840
Huh?

00:11:21.840 --> 00:11:23.070
That's...

00:11:30.080 --> 00:11:33.000
Why is the facility currently in the sky?

00:11:33.370 --> 00:11:38.250
That's because the research facility needed an alchemist...

00:11:38.250 --> 00:11:42.300
Whose bloodline is registered to serve as its management interface.

00:11:43.550 --> 00:11:49.330
Flameu was chosen and taken in.

00:11:56.900 --> 00:12:01.130
As an immortal management interface,

00:12:01.130 --> 00:12:05.290
Flameu continued her research for many years.

00:12:05.290 --> 00:12:08.830
However, since she couldn't determine the influence of humans on the environment,

00:12:08.830 --> 00:12:13.720
she concluded them to be a confounding factor across her research.

00:12:30.520 --> 00:12:33.810
Despite our opposition,

00:12:35.600 --> 00:12:39.150
the facility lifted into the sky where it could not be reached.

00:12:49.530 --> 00:12:56.340
In other words, if other humans were there,
she wouldn't be able to obtain the results she wanted.

00:12:56.340 --> 00:13:00.130
Hey, Clone, why can Nio-san hear her voice?

00:13:02.000 --> 00:13:04.480
According to the records,

00:13:04.480 --> 00:13:09.790
management interfaces can sense each others' minds.

00:13:10.950 --> 00:13:13.570
But Nio-san is a normal girl, isn't she?

00:13:13.570 --> 00:13:15.390
Well...

00:13:16.460 --> 00:13:20.910
Actually there was a time when I became an interface.

00:13:20.910 --> 00:13:23.860
Though, my sister was helping me back then.

00:13:23.860 --> 00:13:26.100
Is that so?

00:13:26.100 --> 00:13:30.530
Clone-san, is it really not possible to release her?

00:13:31.340 --> 00:13:33.790
Unfortunately, that is impossible.

00:13:34.740 --> 00:13:39.460
Flameu has a very strong will and is fixated on the research facility.

00:13:39.830 --> 00:13:43.840
I doubt she will leave it on her own.

00:13:44.460 --> 00:13:48.840
Also, as she's spent too long as a management interface,

00:13:49.250 --> 00:13:53.860
her body is most likely no longer human.

00:13:53.860 --> 00:13:55.530
Hey Clone,

00:13:55.530 --> 00:13:59.660
The Adventures of the Hummingbird Princess are written about her, right?

00:13:59.660 --> 00:14:02.800
I realised it after hearing what you said.

00:14:02.800 --> 00:14:03.280
Yes.

00:14:03.750 --> 00:14:09.240
The reason it felt nostalgic was because I've known her since I was little.

00:14:09.680 --> 00:14:13.570
Hey, what is that picture book about?

00:14:17.500 --> 00:14:18.710
Here it is.

00:14:21.310 --> 00:14:22.810
I'll read it.

00:14:25.070 --> 00:14:27.310
A long time ago, in a place far away,

00:14:27.310 --> 00:14:30.720
there was a girl known as the Hummingbird Princess.

00:14:32.030 --> 00:14:38.190
A girl was found crying one day because she was unable to grow vegetables.

00:14:38.190 --> 00:14:43.520
The Hummingbird Princess came along with a mysterious watering can,

00:14:43.520 --> 00:14:46.610
used it to water the vegetables, and they quickly recovered.

00:14:46.610 --> 00:14:50.490
However, the field soon withered.

00:14:50.490 --> 00:14:55.660
"While you water the field, I'll go figure out why this is happening,"

00:14:56.060 --> 00:14:59.900
said the Hummingbird Princess as she departed on an adventure.

00:15:03.050 --> 00:15:07.530
After completing her adventure, the Hummingbird Princess returned.

00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:11.000
The fields were worse than they were before she left.

00:15:11.000 --> 00:15:16.850
The Hummingbird Princess shared the data and tools she gathered on her adventure with the people of the town.

00:15:17.260 --> 00:15:20.430
But the fields would not return to how they were before.

00:15:20.430 --> 00:15:25.570
The mysterious watering can had been overused on the fields.

00:15:25.570 --> 00:15:27.830
"Don't use the watering can any more."

00:15:27.830 --> 00:15:30.290
"Let the fields rest."

00:15:30.290 --> 00:15:34.430
But the people of the town would not stop using the watering can.

00:15:34.430 --> 00:15:40.870
The people of the town had become unable to tend the fields without the use of such a convenient tool.

00:15:40.870 --> 00:15:42.720
"Why don't they understand?"

00:15:42.720 --> 00:15:43.940
"Why?"

00:15:43.940 --> 00:15:45.040
"I don't understand."

00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:47.340
"I just don't understand!"

00:15:48.510 --> 00:15:50.500
The picture books end here.

00:15:50.500 --> 00:15:56.460
Since I was separated from her, I couldn't continue the story.

00:15:56.460 --> 00:15:58.080
I see.

00:15:58.080 --> 00:16:01.850
As you said, it certainly seems like a hopeless situation.

00:16:01.850 --> 00:16:04.310
No, this is not the end!

00:16:05.310 --> 00:16:06.320
Is that so?

00:16:07.710 --> 00:16:09.590
There is no way that is true.

00:16:09.590 --> 00:16:14.330
There was no other way for me to write this story.

00:16:14.330 --> 00:16:17.040
No, the story continues.

00:16:17.040 --> 00:16:18.580
I still remember it.

00:16:22.170 --> 00:16:23.370
I can't find it.

00:16:24.230 --> 00:16:26.800
Is it really in here?

00:16:26.800 --> 00:16:27.710
Yes.

00:16:27.710 --> 00:16:30.440
Okay, leave it to me.

00:16:30.440 --> 00:16:33.680
Come out, crystal ball!

00:16:34.200 --> 00:16:36.700
Tell us where the picture book is!

00:16:43.420 --> 00:16:44.760
There it is!

00:16:44.760 --> 00:16:45.850
It's over there.

00:16:52.570 --> 00:16:54.610
You found it! This is it!

00:16:58.980 --> 00:17:02.950
Doesn't the art look a bit different than before?

00:17:02.950 --> 00:17:05.630
Did Clone-san draw this?

00:17:06.430 --> 00:17:10.130
I can't remember anything other than that my mum gave it to me.

00:17:10.940 --> 00:17:12.390
Miria did?

00:17:14.300 --> 00:17:17.720
Out of ideas, the Hummingbird Princess cried alone.

00:17:18.220 --> 00:17:22.330
But there was a girl who noticed.

00:17:23.260 --> 00:17:24.980
"I'm sorry, Hummingbird Princess."

00:17:25.520 --> 00:17:28.560
"You've always been helping me."

00:17:31.450 --> 00:17:34.150
"That's why, this time I'll help you."

00:17:34.840 --> 00:17:37.410
"Everyone, please help me out."

00:17:38.180 --> 00:17:39.910
"Come, Hummingbird Princess."

00:17:39.910 --> 00:17:42.160
"Let's make a new watering can together."

00:17:42.160 --> 00:17:45.540
"If everyone works together, we can make a better one."

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:46.670
"Okay."

00:17:46.670 --> 00:17:51.420
"Let's make a new watering can and plant flowers everywhere!"

00:17:51.420 --> 00:17:55.530
And so the Hummingbird Princess worked with everyone to make a new watering can...

00:17:55.530 --> 00:17:58.470
...and fill the town with flowers.

00:17:58.470 --> 00:18:00.800
And they lived happily ever after.

00:18:01.710 --> 00:18:03.640
This was back from when...

00:18:03.640 --> 00:18:05.390
What a nice story.

00:18:05.390 --> 00:18:06.120
Yeah.

00:18:06.120 --> 00:18:07.930
Everyone ends up happy.

00:18:07.930 --> 00:18:10.610
I loved this ending.

00:18:10.840 --> 00:18:13.090
But it's a bit forced.

00:18:13.090 --> 00:18:16.370
Suddenly the girl with the hat became the protagonist.

00:18:16.370 --> 00:18:17.830
That's true.

00:18:17.830 --> 00:18:21.820
Hey, maybe this was written by Escha's mother.

00:18:21.820 --> 00:18:23.170
That makes sense.

00:18:23.170 --> 00:18:24.790
I'm sure that's it, Escha-chan.

00:18:25.090 --> 00:18:26.750
Eh? Mum did?

00:18:27.140 --> 00:18:28.830
Yes, Escha.

00:18:28.830 --> 00:18:32.070
This was certainly written by Miria.

00:18:32.070 --> 00:18:36.770
You didn't like the ending I wrote and started crying.

00:18:36.770 --> 00:18:39.350
So that's what happened...

00:18:40.120 --> 00:18:41.720
Miria was amazing.

00:18:41.720 --> 00:18:45.480
She could even create stories.

00:18:45.770 --> 00:18:48.690
The story mum wrote...

00:18:48.900 --> 00:18:53.590
Your mother was probably just as bubbly as you are.

00:18:53.590 --> 00:18:55.440
What a good mother you had, Escha-chan.

00:18:56.080 --> 00:18:57.150
Yeah.

00:18:59.320 --> 00:19:04.720
Hey Clone, let's ensure Flameu-chan receives the same happy ending.

00:19:05.330 --> 00:19:07.810
I want to save Flameu-chan!

00:19:07.810 --> 00:19:08.790
Me too.

00:19:08.790 --> 00:19:11.080
I want to tell her that she's wrong.

00:19:11.080 --> 00:19:14.540
After hearing all this, I'll come along too.

00:19:15.570 --> 00:19:18.810
Thank you, everyone!

00:19:18.810 --> 00:19:21.260
Come with us, Clone-san.

00:19:21.540 --> 00:19:27.160
I don't think I can be of much use.

00:19:27.160 --> 00:19:30.760
She has probably forgotten about me already.

00:19:30.760 --> 00:19:32.520
That's not true!

00:19:32.520 --> 00:19:36.330
If you were that important to Flameu-chan, she'll remember you!

00:19:36.330 --> 00:19:37.400
That's true!

00:19:37.990 --> 00:19:39.580
Back then...

00:19:41.060 --> 00:19:44.530
...I also remembered my sister.

00:19:48.970 --> 00:19:50.400
Please, Clone.

00:19:50.400 --> 00:19:53.130
Let's go to Flameu-chan together.

00:19:53.130 --> 00:19:54.040
But...

00:19:58.530 --> 00:20:01.260
Actually, even back then,

00:20:01.580 --> 00:20:06.300
the Malier family's alchemists didn't want to be separated from Flameu either.

00:20:07.340 --> 00:20:08.340
If I think about it,

00:20:08.340 --> 00:20:13.760
they were the ones that helped with the apple tree I had planted.

00:20:15.320 --> 00:20:20.460
They tended it with me for many years.

00:20:22.790 --> 00:20:25.490
Everyone helped out and worked together.

00:20:25.950 --> 00:20:27.700
They were wonderful people.

00:20:28.400 --> 00:20:31.790
Even though I was with these people for such a long time,

00:20:32.180 --> 00:20:33.670
I'm still no good.

00:20:33.670 --> 00:20:34.960
Clone?

00:20:36.470 --> 00:20:37.420
I understand.

00:20:37.820 --> 00:20:41.720
Please let me join you when you go see her.

00:20:41.720 --> 00:20:42.880
Yeah!

00:20:43.630 --> 00:20:46.370
We'll save Flameu-chan no matter what!

00:20:49.520 --> 00:20:51.810
Escha, I need you to do me a favour.

00:20:52.850 --> 00:20:54.810
I want you to synthesize this.

00:20:55.810 --> 00:20:57.270
This is...

00:20:57.850 --> 00:21:00.750
We'll need it to save Flameu.

00:21:01.160 --> 00:21:05.460
It's a complicated recipe, but now that you have made so many things,

00:21:05.460 --> 00:21:06.530
I know you can do it.

00:21:07.570 --> 00:21:09.490
Logy-san!

00:21:09.490 --> 00:21:10.870
I understand.

00:21:10.870 --> 00:21:11.790
Leave it to me!

00:21:13.160 --> 00:21:17.250
All right, I have to work on this guy.

00:21:50.960 --> 00:21:53.120
It's finally time, Logy-san.

00:21:53.120 --> 00:21:54.570
Yeah.

00:21:54.570 --> 00:21:58.000
Flameu-chan, we're coming for you!
